- **Co-run headroom is unmitigated.** Physical RAM is 495 GiB; the two caps sum to 600 GiB. At the predecessor's 9,000 s stop the pair held ~111 + ~130 GB. Over a cap eight times longer the OOM killer could fire before either configured cap. I left the caps as specified — the harvest must read `runner.rc`/`caprun.json` to tell a cap stop from an OOM kill.
